The MnWO₄ common-Uiso branch is not identifiable: its Uiso and polarization correlate at 95.7%, for only a 0.006%-point Rwp change. I’m rejecting that branch and retaining the published positive-definite Mn/W displacement tensors. The accepted model is correlation-clean (only one 0.904 cell-metric correlation) at Rwp 2.9243%, and I’m now exporting all deliverables from that exact checkpoint.

The final project has also passed an independent atomic forward replay: all three saved structures and fractions reproduce the full 8,301-point grid at Rwp 2.92430%, with no negative ADPs, widths, background, or polarization flags. I’m doing one last final-state trace-Mn₃O₄ sensitivity test so the report can distinguish “absent” from “not independently resolvable.”

